/-!
# Global generation over a separably closed field

Source: the Weil conjectures blueprint, chapter `sec-smooth-purity`, unit
`sk-prop-sf-kunneth-ordinary`, lemma `lem-kun-03qu-global-generation`, order 1695
(blueprint: lem-kun-03qu-global-generation).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

/-- Every abelian sheaf on the small étale site of the spectrum of a separably closed
field is generated by its global sections.
Source: blueprint `lem-kun-03qu-global-generation`, order 1695
(blueprint: lem-kun-03qu-global-generation).

Proof:
1. A separably closed field is a strictly henselian local ring: its maximal ideal is
   zero, the henselian condition for that ideal is immediate, and its residue field
   is itself (`def-kun-separably-closed`, `def-weil-pbc-henselian-terminology`).
   Apply `lem-weil-pbc-strictly-henselian-sections-stalk` with R = K to identify
   global sections with the stalk at each geometric point of Spec K.
2. Let epsilon be the canonical evaluation of `def-kun-global-generated`. For a
   stalk element a, the preceding germ isomorphism supplies a global section s
   with germ a. In the constant integer summand indexed by s, take the canonical
   section 1, include it into the coproduct, and take its germ. By the defining
   evaluation formula and naturality of germs (`def-weil-pbc-geometric-stalks`),
   epsilon sends this germ to the germ of s, namely a. Thus evaluation is
   surjective on each geometric stalk. In the delivered constant-free-group
   model of the coproduct, this section is the basis element indexed by s.
3. The criterion `lem-kun-global-generated-stalkwise`, specialized to integer
   coefficients, makes evaluation an epimorphism. This is precisely
   `IsGloballyGeneratedAbelianEtaleSheaf F`. -/
theorem isGloballyGeneratedAbelianEtaleSheaf_of_isSepClosed
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsSepClosed K]
    (F : Sheaf (Spec (.of K)).smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    IsGloballyGeneratedAbelianEtaleSheaf F := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
